  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;MUNICIPALITY OF KATWA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Municipality of Katwa is a governing entity established on 1 April 1869, responsible for managing the town of Katwa."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KATWA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Katwa is a sub-divisional town in Purba Bardhaman district, West Bengal, India, known for its urbanization due to railroad construction and its significant population growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Katwa is a town within the Katwa subdivision, covering 1,070.48 km² and having a population of 963,022 with a density of 900/km² in 2011."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;10TH ACT OF MUNICIPAL RULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 10th Act of Municipal Rules established the Municipality of Katwa, marking a formal governance structure for the town."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAILROAD CONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Railroad construction in Katwa, including Katwa-Azimganj (1903), Katwa-Bandel (1912), Katwa-Bardhaman (1915), and Katwa-Ahmedpur (1917), significantly boosted urbanization."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2011 CENSUS OF INDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2011 Census of India recorded a total population of 81,615 in Katwa, with 41,350 males and 40,265 females, and 6,799 children below 6 years old."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITERACY RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"As per the 2011 Census of India, the literacy rate in Katwa was 79.87%, with 65,187 literate individuals over 6 years of age."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAM CARREY JUNIOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Carrey Junior is commemorated by a tomb in Katwa, indicating his historical significance to the area."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PURBA BARDHAMAN DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Purba Bardhaman district is the specific district where the Katwa subdivision is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Purba Bardhaman district is where Katwa is located, and it is part of the larger Bardhaman district in West Bengal, India."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEST BENGAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"West Bengal is a state in India, containing the district of Purba Bardhaman."&lt;SEP&gt;"West Bengal is the state in India where Katwa is situated, known for its diverse culture and history."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARDHAMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bardhaman is a district in West Bengal, containing both the original and the bifurcated parts of the district, including Katwa."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOK SABHA CONSTITUENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Katwa is part of the Bardhaman Purba Lok Sabha constituency, representing the area in the national parliament."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIDHAN SABHA CONSTITUENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Katwa is also part of the Katwa Vidhan Sabha constituency, representing the area in the state legislature."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBDIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Katwa subdivision was formed after the bifurcation of Bardhaman district in 2017, with a total population of 963,022."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AJAY RIVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ajay River flows through the Katwa subdivision, joining the Bhagirathi river."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KANKSA-KETUGRAM PLAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kanksa-Ketugram plain is part of the geographical area covered by the Katwa subdivision."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BHAGIRATHI BASIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bhagirathi basin is another geographical feature within the Katwa subdivision."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARDHAMAN DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bardhaman district is the larger administrative division that includes the Katwa subdivision."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARDHAMAN SADAR NORTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bardhaman Sadar North is a subdivision within the larger Bardhaman Sadar area, covering 1,958.43 km² and having a population of 1,586,623 with 73.58% rural and 26.42% urban population in 2011."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bardhaman Sadar North is one of the administrative subdivisions within the Purba Bardhaman district."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARDHAMAN SADAR SOUTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bardhaman Sadar South is another administrative subdivision within the Purba Bardhaman district."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bardhaman Sadar South is another subdivision within the larger Bardhaman Sadar area, covering 1,410.03 km² and having a population of 1,198,155 with 95.54% rural and 4.46% urban population in 2011."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KALNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kalna is a town within the Kalna subdivision, covering 993.75 km² and having a population of 1,087,732 with a density of 1,099/km² in 2011."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kalna is another administrative subdivision within the Purba Bardhaman district."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0127-61a0b15852a5</data>
    </node>
